Market Challenges
Retrofitting liquid cooling into operating data centres involves complex coordination between rack-level equipment and existing facility infrastructure. Providers must manage coolant distribution units, cold plates, piping interfaces, leak detection, and commissioning requirements while working around established operational procedures.

Project scheduling can also be difficult because customers need to limit downtime and coordinate installation activities across multiple technical teams. Differences in legacy infrastructure and facility layouts make standardised deployment approaches challenging.

Market Restraints
Outage risks and water-loop integration complexity remain major barriers to wider adoption. Data centre operators must protect expensive computing equipment from leaks, fluid-related failures, and disruptions during installation.

Limited availability of qualified technicians and restricted site access can further delay projects. Retrofit costs and the need to demonstrate measurable operational benefits may also lead some buyers to postpone upgrades or adopt phased implementation strategies.

